    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 65002', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp 65002', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65002\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200\\naddress-family ipv4 unicast\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nexit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Starts BGP process with AS 65002\\n2. Configures the neighbor 10.2.1.2 in AS 200\\n3. Activates IPv4 unicast address family for the neighbor\\n4. Exits address-family configuration mode\\n\\nNote that the export policy (EXPORT_DIRECT) would need to be separately configured in Cisco using route-maps or distribution lists.\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 65002'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65002\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200\\naddress-family ipv4 unicast\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nexit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Starts BGP process with AS 65002\\n2. Configures the neighbor 10.2.1.2 in AS 200\\n3. Activates IPv4 unicast address family for the neighbor\\n4. Exits address-family configuration mode\\n\\nNote that the export policy (EXPORT_DIRECT) would need to be separately configured in Cisco using route-maps or distribution lists.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'address-family ipv4 unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65002\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200\\naddress-family ipv4 unicast\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nexit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Starts BGP process with AS 65002\\n2. Configures the neighbor 10.2.1.2 in AS 200\\n3. Activates IPv4 unicast address family for the neighbor\\n4. Exits address-family configuration mode\\n\\nNote that the export policy (EXPORT_DIRECT) would need to be separately configured in Cisco using route-maps or distribution lists.\", 'trans_template': 'address-family ipv4 unicast'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 activate', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65002\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200\\naddress-family ipv4 unicast\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nexit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Starts BGP process with AS 65002\\n2. Configures the neighbor 10.2.1.2 in AS 200\\n3. Activates IPv4 unicast address family for the neighbor\\n4. Exits address-family configuration mode\\n\\nNote that the export policy (EXPORT_DIRECT) would need to be separately configured in Cisco using route-maps or distribution lists.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 activate'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'exit-address-family', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65002\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 200\\naddress-family ipv4 unicast\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nexit-address-family\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco configuration:\\n1. Starts BGP process with AS 65002\\n2. Configures the neighbor 10.2.1.2 in AS 200\\n3. Activates IPv4 unicast address family for the neighbor\\n4. Exits address-family configuration mode\\n\\nNote that the export policy (EXPORT_DIRECT) would need to be separately configured in Cisco using route-maps or distribution lists.\", 'trans_template': 'exit-address-family'}]]": 1,
    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map EXPORT_DIRECT permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 65002'], 'root': 'router bgp 65002', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT_DIRECT permit 10\\n match interface \\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `policy-statement` maps to `route-map`\\n- `term 1` maps to sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` maps to `match interface` (which matches directly connected routes)\\n- The implicit `then accept` is represented by `permit` in the route-map statement\\n\\nNote: The actual interface matching would need to be specified more precisely in a real Cisco implementation, as `match interface` alone would match all directly connected interfaces. The Juniper command matches all direct routes regardless of interface.\", 'trans_template': 'route-map EXPORT_DIRECT permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match interface', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 65002'], 'root': 'router bgp 65002', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT_DIRECT permit 10\\n match interface \\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `policy-statement` maps to `route-map`\\n- `term 1` maps to sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` maps to `match interface` (which matches directly connected routes)\\n- The implicit `then accept` is represented by `permit` in the route-map statement\\n\\nNote: The actual interface matching would need to be specified more precisely in a real Cisco implementation, as `match interface` alone would match all directly connected interfaces. The Juniper command matches all direct routes regardless of interface.\", 'trans_template': 'match interface'}]]": 1,
